ROMX $2E
	; Selectable player character. "Player Sprites" holds every overworld sheet
	; the player can be assigned (plus bike/surf) so LoadPlayerSpriteGraphics can
	; keep using a single BANK(RedSprite).
	"Player Sprites"
	"Player Appearance"
	; Displaced from banks $13 and $C by the player pics. Both are reached
	; through bank-resolving dispatch (BANK(GetPredefPointer) / jpfar), so
	; neither cares which bank it lives in.
	"Predefs"
	"Battle Engine 6"
	; Both pinned here 2026-08-14, for the same reason: left floating, rgblink
	; first-fit drops a small section into whichever tight bank happens to have
	; room, and it can pick a DIFFERENT bank per build target. "Random" ($45
	; bytes) had landed in bank $1, taking it from $52 free to $0d. "Extra
	; Options Menu" ($67 bytes) then landed in bank $1 in the release build but
	; bank $7 in _DEBUG - and bank $7 is already one of the two that shrink most
	; under _DEBUG. Both are reached only by farcall, so BANK() resolves wherever
	; they sit. Pin small floating sections; do not trust first-fit.
	"Random"
	"Extra Options Menu"
ROMX $33
	; AUDIO_4 - new bank added by the Shin/Yellow-style audio-engine import
	; (SHIN_IMPORT_PLAN.md Phase 1.1). All of AUDIO_4's pieces must land in
	; the same physical bank (its PlaySound/SFX headers/engine code address
	; each other bank-relatively, same as AUDIO_1/2/3 do in their own banks),
	; so - per this file's own $2E rule above - it is pinned explicitly rather
	; than left floating. $2F-$3F was entirely unallocated before this.
	"Sound Effect Headers 4"
	"Music Headers 4"
	"Sound Effects 4"
	"Audio Engine 4"
	"Music 4"
